  "statement": {
    "representation": "pdf-text-entry",
    "text": "Let G be a finitely generated group such that for every element g ∈ G the\nset of commutators {[x, g] | x ∈ G} is a subgroup of G. Is it true that G is residually\nnilpotent?\n    The answer is affirmative if G is finite.            D. Gonçalves, T. Nasybullov",
